age_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"df6e418e-895c-4a85-bcfa-aec85477de61"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：时空轨迹。场景ID：spatiotemporal_trajectory\n识别场景：时空轨迹 (spatiotemporal_trajectory)；场景模式：single；候选场景：spatiotemporal_trajectory\n任务切分：\n- 请读取这个本地视频的时长、分辨率、帧率和时间信息，整理成后续分析可以使用的标准输入。测试视频路径是 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4。\n任务规划：\n1. 调用多媒体解析工具访问本地视频文件 /mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4，提取其核心元数据指标，包括视频总时长、画面分辨率、播放帧率及时间戳信息。\n2. 对提取的视频参数进行清洗与标准化转换，按照时空轨迹分析场景的输入规范重构数据结构，输出可供下游分析模块直接调用的标准输入格式。\n场景任务：\n- spatiotemporal_trajectory: 我将读取本地视频/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4的时长、分辨率、帧率和时间信息，并整理成后续分析可以使用的标准输入。；参数：{'分析对象': '本地视频 (/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4)', '分析目标': '视频时长、分辨率、帧率和时间信息读取与整理'}\n已提取参数：{'分析对象': '本地视频 (/mnt/datasets/Vedio-demo/Trafic.mp4)', '分析目标': '视频时长、分辨率、帧率和时间信息读取与整理'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：分析对象。轨迹主体，如人员、车辆、设备、事件、案件对象等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。需要分析的起止时间、日期、时段或相对时间\n- 提取可选参数：空间范围。轨迹涉及的区域、道路、地点、围栏或行政区划\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。轨迹回放、停留点识别、路径分析、异常轨迹、同行分析、活动范围分析等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"15910c37-e076-4b57-889c-9c3f29aa165a"},{"content":"我来提取该视频的元数据信息。先使用 Python 脚本读取视频文件的核心参数。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":278,"prompt_tokens":12561,"total_tokens":12839,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":204,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":278},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":12561}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-79e1f9d5-937b-908a-b94d-a5c5ae69519d","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8e48-9425-7873-8abf-0b2ad54896d7-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"which ffprobe || which ffmpeg","description":"检查系统中是否安装了 ffprobe/ffmpeg"},"id":"call_feb5d17521454266b6171377","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":12561,"output_tokens":278,"total_tokens":12839,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":204}}},{"content":"/usr/bin/ffprobe","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"5803eb61-030c-469e-b9f2-548995849e4e","tool_call_id":"call_feb5d17521454266b6171377","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"comp